# Project One Move-Between-Rooms Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: conceptual support for M6; movement design for M7
#
# Review the course-provided movement flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, WHILE, SET, or similar terms.

START

Set currentRoom = "Submarine Dock"

Display the current room.
Display the available directions.
Display the player's inventory.

WHILE the game is running:

    Ask the player:
        "Which direction would you like to move?"
        "Enter north, south, east, or west."

    Get the player's input.

    Convert the input to lowercase.

    IF input = "north":

        IF north is available from the current room:
            Move the player north.
            Update currentRoom.
            Display the new room.

        ELSE:
            Display "You cannot go north from here."

    ELSE IF input = "south":

        IF south is available from the current room:
            Move the player south.
            Update currentRoom.
            Display the new room.

        ELSE:
            Display "You cannot go south from here."

    ELSE IF input = "east":

        IF east is available from the current room:
            Move the player east.
            Update currentRoom.
            Display the new room.

        ELSE:
            Display "You cannot go east from here."

    ELSE IF input = "west":

        IF west is available from the current room:
            Move the player west.
            Update currentRoom.
            Display the new room.

        ELSE:
            Display "You cannot go west from here."

    ELSE:

        Display "Invalid direction."
        Display "Please enter north, south, east, or west."

    IF currentRoom = "Deep Sea Trench":

        IF all six items are in the player's inventory:

            Display "You collected everything needed to escape!"
            Display "The Kraken cannot stop you!"
            Display "YOU WIN!"

            End the game.

        ELSE:

            Display "The Kraken attacks!"
            Display "You did not collect all of the items."
            Display "GAME OVER."

            End the game.

END WHILE
